<title>SINGAPORE: Kay Hian first half net profit up 1.9pct.</title>
<headline>Kay Hian first half net profit up 1.9pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in million Singapore dollars unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>						  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Net profit				21.39  vs    21.00</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)		   4.87  vs     4.78</p>
<p>    Dividend   (cents)		     0.75  vs     0.75</p>
<p>    Turnover				  69.01  vs    56.15</p>
<p>    Other income			     2.19  vs     3.36</p>
<p>    Operating profit			24.92  vs    27.08</p>
<p>    Share of profit from associates    5.67  vs     2.57</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  30.59  vs    29.65</p>
<p>    Tax					  9.20  vs     8.66</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date   October 8, 1996</p>
<p>    Dividend register   September 23, 1996</p>
<p>Note - Stockbrokers Kay Hian Holdings Ltd said its percentage increase in net profit is less the percentage increase in turnover because of higher provisions in stocks, doubtful debts and contingencies.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
